\section{Regime Topology Breakdown}

The state space is partitioned into three distinct geometric regions based on local values of $\mathrm{Ri}_b$:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{\color{gsptblue}Active Turbulent Branch ($\mathrm{Ri}_b < \mathrm{Ri}_{\text{trans}}$):} Shear production dominates; system remains fully coupled.
    \item \textbf{\color{gsptorange}Bistable Hysteresis Region ($\mathrm{Ri}_{\text{trans}} \le \mathrm{Ri}_b \le \mathrm{Ri}_{\text{fold}}$):} System exhibits history-dependent bistability governed by canard dynamics.
    \item \textbf{\color{gsptred}Collapsed Branch ($\mathrm{Ri}_b > \mathrm{Ri}_{\text{fold}}$):} Normal hyperbolicity fails; surface thermally decouples.
\end{enumerate}

